{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_4>\nn, m = map(int, input().split())\nvalues = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\nimport bisect\n\nsplit_point = n // 2\nleft_vals = []\nright_vals = []\n\ndef explore_left(index, current):\n    if index == split_point:\n        left_vals.append(current % m)\n    else:\n        explore_left(index + 1, (current + values[index]) % m)\n        explore_left(index + 1, current)\n\ndef explore_right(index, current):\n    if index == n:\n        right_vals.append(current % m)\n    else:\n        explore_right(index + 1, (current + values[index]) % m)\n        explore_right(index + 1, current)\n\nexplore_left(0, 0)\nexplore_right(split_point, 0)\n\nleft_unique = sorted(set(left_vals))\nmax_total = 0\n\nfor right_val in right_vals:\n    req = m - right_val\n    position = bisect.bisect_left(left_unique, req)\n    for offset in [0, -1]:\n        if 0 <= position + offset < len(left_unique):\n            total = (left_unique[position + offset] + right_val) % m\n            if total > max_total:\n                max_total = total\n\nprint(max_total)\n</your_rewritten_code_4>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <set>\n#include <cmath>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nint n, m;\nvector<int> values;\nvector<int> left_vals;\nvector<int> right_vals;\n\nvoid explore_left(int index, int current) {\n    if (index == n / 2) {\n        left_vals.push_back(current % m);\n    } else {\n        explore_left(index + 1, (current + values[index]) % m);\n        explore_left(index + 1, current);\n    }\n}\n\nvoid explore_right(int index, int current) {\n    if (index == n) {\n        right_vals.push_back(current % m);\n    } else {\n        explore_right(index + 1, (current + values[index]) % m);\n        explore_right(index + 1, current);\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n    cin >> n >> m;\n    values.resize(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        cin >> values[i];\n    }\n\n    explore_left(0, 0);\n    explore_right(n / 2, 0);\n\n    set<int> left_set(left_vals.begin(), left_vals.end());\n    vector<int> left_unique(left_set.begin(), left_set.end());\n    sort(left_unique.begin(), left_unique.end());\n\n    int max_total = 0;\n    for (int right_val : right_vals) {\n        int req = m - right_val;\n        auto it = lower_bound(left_unique.begin(), left_unique.end(), req);\n        int position = it - left_unique.begin();\n        \n        for (int offset : {0, -1}) {\n            if (0 <= position + offset && position + offset < (int)left_unique.size()) {\n                int total = (left_unique[position + offset] + right_val) % m;\n                if (total > max_total) {\n                    max_total = total;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    cout << max_total << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0001358893496217206, -2.50339189733495e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, 